<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Education and Learning – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Education and Learning</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> Next Trimester, I Plan to Learn...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write a short report on a class activity. Interactive: Edit classmates' narratives for clarity and coherence.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a short report on a class learning activity (e.g., "Today, we are discussing famous leaders. First, we read about their achievements. Then, we answered questions."). Can write a summary of the main points learned in a history lesson (e.g., "Three main points are: Panama's independence, the construction of the Panama Canal, and indigenous peoples and cultures."). Can edit a peer's short narrative for clarity (e.g., add, "in 2025" to make the date clear).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; text-align: left;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 34%; text-align: left;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; text-align: left;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students and displays images of various school subjects (e.g., math, history, computer science, English). Students are asked to quickly write down two subjects they enjoy and one skill they want to develop in the next trimester. They show their written lists to a classmate. This activates prior knowledge related to the theme "Next Trimester, I Plan to Learn..." and the vocabulary (subjects, skills, develop).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a short sentence on the board about their own plan, for example: "Next trimester, I am learning new teaching skills." and "I would like to study more about digital education." The teacher models the pronunciation, specifically stressing "I *am* learn-ing" and "I *would* like" while pointing to the words. The teacher demonstrates writing a simple 3-sentence report about yesterday's class activity, focusing on sequential ideas: "Yesterday, we discussed career goals. First, we learned new vocabulary. Then, we talked about different jobs. Finally, we shared our own goals."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Am I talking about something happening now or in the future when I say 'I *am* learning' in this context?" (Expected answer: In the future, a plan/ongoing action.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I *would* like to study,' does it mean I *have* to study, or I *want* to study?" (Expected answer: I want to study, a desire.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Education and Learning".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher distributes a short written text, a sample "Class Activity Report" from a hypothetical 8th-grade student. The report is about a recent history lesson and includes the target grammar and vocabulary. Example:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                    "<b>Our History Lesson Summary</b><br>
                    Today, we actively discussed Panama's history. First, our teacher showed us pictures of the Panama Canal's construction. We were interested in learning about the different stages. Then, we read about indigenous peoples and cultures. Many classmates are developing critical thinking skills by asking questions. I would like to study more about this subject because it's educational. My career goals include understanding more about my country's past. We are achieving a lot of knowledge!"
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Writing: Can understand the structure and content of a short report or summary of a class activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main topic of this report?" (Expected answer: Panama's history lesson).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "The students only looked at pictures of the Panama Canal." (False) "The student wants to learn more about the subject." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match phrases from the report to their meanings (e.g., "actively discussed" to "talked a lot," "developing critical thinking skills" to "learning to think deeply").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">7-9 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Focusing on writing accurate sentences using Present Continuous for ongoing actions, Gerunds after prepositions, and Modals for ability/desires. Utilizing target vocabulary: education, skills, knowledge, learn, study, develop, grow, achieve, academic, motivated, actively, well.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from a class report. They complete the sentences using given vocabulary words or the correct grammatical form (e.g., "She is interested in _______ (learn) about scholarships." → "She is interested in learning about scholarships."). They also complete sentences with modals: "Next trimester, I _______ to develop my English skills." (would like/want).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Guided Paragraph Writing:</b> Students work individually to write three to five sentences about a *past* class activity (e.g., a science experiment, a reading session) using prompts like: "Today we learned...", "First, we...", "Then, we...", "Many students are...", "I would like...". They must use at least one present continuous verb, one gerund after a preposition, and one modal verb, and at least three of the target vocabulary words (e.g., knowledge, actively, educational, skills). The teacher circulates, offering support and ensuring correct formation.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Peer Sentence Check:</b> Students exchange their written sentences from the previous activity with a partner. Each student reads their partner's sentences aloud to themselves first, focusing on pronunciation, especially stress patterns in modals ("I *would* like") and continuous forms ("I *am* learn-ing"). They then discreetly check for clarity, coherence, and basic spelling/grammar errors. They gently point out one or two corrections needed to their partner, for instance, by asking "Is this word 'skill' or 'skull'? What sound is that /ɪ/ or /iː/?" to practice phonemic awareness, or suggest "You should keep practicing to make your sentences clearer."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Education and Learning".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Written Product & Peer Editing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in pairs to produce a short report (4-6 sentences) about a *recent class activity*, such as a group project, a discussion, or a lab session. The report should describe what they did and what they learned, incorporating their plans for developing related skills in the next trimester. They must use at least one instance of the present continuous for an ongoing action/future plan, one gerund after a preposition, and one modal for desire. They should also include at least five target vocabulary words (e.g., trimester, achieve, knowledge, academic, schedule, motivated, curious). For example, "Last week, we studied history. We are interested in learning about local culture. Our classmate, Maria, is actively developing her research skills. I would like to improve my writing skills next trimester. We are planning to achieve excellent grades."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After writing their draft report, pairs exchange their report with another pair. Each pair then acts as "editors" for the other's report, focusing on clarity, coherence, and correct use of the target grammar and vocabulary. They should look for opportunities to make the narrative clearer (e.g., suggesting adding a specific date or detail, "add 'in 2025' to make the date clear"). They will provide written feedback and then briefly discuss their suggestions respectfully with the other pair, engaging in discussions about personal and learning goals and offering relevant suggestions for improvement.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students finalize their class activity report based on peer feedback and then submit their edited report along with the peer feedback they provided to another group.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation/Rubric):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and Coherence: Is the report easy to understand? (A2.3: Can connect sentences into a coherent text).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of Target Grammar: Correct application of Present Continuous, Gerunds after prepositions, and Modals for desires.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of Target Vocabulary: Appropriate and varied use of learned vocabulary (e.g., education, skills, knowledge, achieve, actively).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Editing Skills: Ability to identify and suggest clear improvements to a peer's narrative for clarity.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sociolinguistic: Engaged in respectful discussions during peer editing.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students write their answers to the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing I learned about writing a report today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did I help my classmates improve their writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing today's report was most challenging for me, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use the new grammar and vocabulary when writing about my future academic goals?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., students were motivated by the peer editing task, the sample report provided a clear model).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., perhaps more explicit instruction on paragraph structure for some students, or additional practice with specific vocabulary items).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the pronunciation points (stress patterns, minimal pairs) effectively integrated? Could they be reinforced more in the next lesson?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will summarize key information from their reports and present their individual next trimester learning goals as part of the 21st Century Skills Project, potentially creating a short visual aid to accompany their summary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>